Wand of polymorph?  Here is my strategy for a good polypile:
1) Go to the mining town level, buy all the tools (candles, lamps and 
   other stuff).  The mining level is a good place because of all of the
   stores, as well as lockable rooms for privacy.  

2) Keep the following tools: towel, key or lock pick, stethoscope, all
   bags,  magic markers and at least one tinning kit.  If you can't
   find a towel, keep a blindfold until you do.Try to identify all
   bags.  Once you find a bag of holding, you only need bags of tricks.
   you don't need anymore bags of holding or sacks, although you might
   want to set aside a bag of holding for a spare.  I feel you should
   keep all bags of tricks as well as wands of create monster.  They are
   good ways to generate monsters for sacraficing at altars.

3) Carry all gems you find here, and then try identify all of them before
   doing the polypile.  That way you can keep the precious ones (which the
   general store keepers or jewelry store keepers will pay lots of money
   for) and polymorph the worthless pieces of glass.

4) Carry all cloaks to the pile(s).  Cloaks are light and not metal.  Too
   much metal in a polypile will cause a iron golem to rise the pile.
   When you polymorph them you hope to get good armor, like the ones I
   listed in the wish list.  You may even want to set aside spares.  I
   very often either over enchant or have destroyed my speed boots and
   gauntlets of power.  Make sure you try on all cloaks that aren't
   hooded to see if they are a good cloak (protection, invisiblility,
   displacement).  If you aren't a priest, make sure you find out what
   items are cursed/blessed by dropping them on the town altar.

5) Split all multiple items up between your two polypiles.  For example
   if you have 6 candles, put 3 in each pile.  

6) Make sure you have identified as much stuff as possible, that way you
   can find which stuff is useful and which isn't.  The mines usually have
   several scrolls of identify, so you shouldn't have much trouble.
   Actually, make sure all of them are blessed.  I play a priest, so this
   isn't that hard, but for a non-Priest, you should find potions of holy
   water before you try to identify lots of stuff.
   If your sure you have enough stuff (armor, tools, potions, scrolls, wands
   and rings) that you aren't going to need in the pile, zap it with the
   wand.

7) Now zap the wand of polymorph.  Kill any golems which rise from the
   rubble.  Then examine it.  Move over a pile, hit ',' and then specify
   that you want to pick up all but prompting for each item.  Choose what
   you feel you need or want to identify.  Polypiles are places to learn
   about unknown items, like wands and tools.

Don't polypile too much, because you wear out your wand of polymorph and
plus your piles get smaller, so there is a smaller chance of getting good
stuff.

There is a lot I didn't discuss.  I could probably write a short book on
polypile strategy for Nethack 3.1, but I won't. (Too late :^O )

